<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. da Vinci returns nine weeks after the diagnosis, about fifteen weeks after the fall. He has worn both splints faithfully and has had fourteen sessions of hand therapy. The numbness of the little finger is much less. His grip is a little stronger, but the ring and little fingers still curl when he reaches for a brush, and he still cannot hold the palette in his right hand for more than a few minutes; fine brushwork with the right hand is beyond him. He draws, writes, and teaches every day with his left hand and paints small panels with a palette fixed to the easel and built-up brushes, with an assistant mixing colors. He takes atorvastatin each evening without muscle aches. He has had no further falls. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Splints and therapy</td><td>Both splints worn; fourteen hand-therapy sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Numbness much less; grip slightly stronger; clawing persists</td></tr><tr><td>Function</td><td>Drawing, writing, and teaching with the left hand; painting small panels with adapted tools</td></tr><tr><td>Statin</td><td>Nine weeks; no muscle aches</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

